  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PERFORMANCE-BASED PARTNERSHIP SCHEME FOCUSING ON QUALITY PROGRAMMING, UNDERSTANDING CHANGE AND RESULTS FOR POOR HOUSEHOLDS AND COMMUNITIES</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teachers are trained in relevant topics such as flood preparedness and response, WASH, and safe behaviours; School alert and risk management committees are established or revitalised; Hazard maps, contingency, mitigation, and evacuation plans are developed in each target school. This project assissted targeted schools to  develop effective DRR Risk Assessments and planning processes and gender-responsive contingency plans in place, with a mapping of seasonal risks such as floods. Teachers were trained on flood prepardness and safe behaviours. Authorities were actively involved in this process.</narrative>
  </description>
